# Rust: security

- Treat external input as untrusted:
  - Validate early at boundaries; convert into validated domain types.
- Avoid parsing into privileged/internal types directly:
  - Prefer DTO → validate → domain conversion.
- Minimize attack surface:
  - Keep dependencies minimal; avoid enabling unnecessary default features.
- Don’t leak secrets:
  - Never log tokens/credentials/PII; avoid including sensitive data in `Debug` output for types that may be logged.
- Prefer constant-time primitives when implementing security-sensitive comparisons or cryptography:
  - Don’t roll your own crypto; use well-reviewed crates and keep interfaces narrow.

